// output says which version produced it. Two streams, by who
// asked: `-V` is an explicit request, so it goes to stdout
// where a script capturing output collects it; unasked-for
// provenance goes to stderr, keeping stdout parseable for the
// commands that emit data there. The `version` subcommand
// prints its own banner as the report's first line, so it
// skips both. Uniform `BANNER` (not the `vc-x1-<sub>` form
// clap's `propagate_version` would print): the version is the
// binary's regardless of which subcommand it routes to.
